This is an independent Rust implementation, not a port of existing code:
the inference engine was written from scratch against ONNX Runtime. The
per-file copyright headers state the same.

What it does depend on, and what stays under its own terms:

  - GLiNER2 model weights — not distributed with this repository.
    The engine loads ONNX exports of GLiNER2 models published by
    Knowledgator (https://huggingface.co/knowledgator). The weights
    remain subject to the licence of their publisher; check it before
    redistributing them with an application.

  - The ONNX conversion scripts under onnx_conversion_scripts/ operate on
    those upstream models and produce derived artefacts. Converting a
    model does not change its licence.

  - ONNX Runtime (https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime) — MIT,
    linked at runtime, not redistributed from here.

GLiNER (Generalist Model for Named Entity Recognition) is the work of
Urchade Zaratiana et al.; GLiNER2 is developed by Knowledgator. This
project implements inference for those models and claims no ownership
over them.
